capability text/graphemes  a text cut into what a reader sees as one character, UAX #29's extended grapheme clusters
  heroes  unicode/segment.graphemes, unicode/segment.grapheme_boundaries
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  unicodedata.iter_graphemes
  note    UAX #29 for Unicode 17.0.0, GB9c's Indic conjuncts included; every line of GraphemeBreakTest.txt 17.0.0 (766) runs as the package's tests. Python answers segments with their indices in code points; here the pieces themselves, or the boundaries as byte indices, which a slice reads. Rust's crate unicode-segmentation is outside the standard library

capability text/grapheme-cursor  the grapheme boundary after or before a place, to move a cursor
  heroes  unicode/segment.next_grapheme_boundary, unicode/segment.previous_grapheme_boundary
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    it reads back only to a boundary no context can undo, so moving a cursor costs about one grapheme, where cutting the whole text costs the text; a place inside a character aborts, as a slice there does

capability class/grapheme-break  the classes UAX #29 cuts graphemes by
  heroes  unicode/segment.grapheme_break_class, unicode/segment.indic_conjunct_break_class
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  unicodedata.grapheme_cluster_break, unicodedata.indic_conjunct_break
  note    the values as `GraphemeBreakProperty.txt` and `DerivedCoreProperties.txt` write them, as Python answers them; held to Python's on all 1,112,064 scalar values by a sweep of 2026-11-17

capability class/extended-pictographic  whether a character is a pictograph, which UAX #29 keeps whole in an emoji sequence
  heroes  unicode/names.has_property
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  unicodedata.extended_pictographic
  note    `names.has_property(c: c, property: "Extended_Pictographic")`: the property is one of the binary properties `unicode/names` reads by name, where the others of `emoji-data.txt` stand too; this package reads it in its own table for GB11 and WB3c

capability text/words  a text cut into words by UAX #29
  heroes  unicode/segment.words, unicode/segment.word_segments, unicode/segment.word_boundaries
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    every line of WordBreakTest.txt 17.0.0 (1,944) runs as the package's tests. `words` keeps the pieces holding a letter, a digit or an ideograph, as Rust's unicode-segmentation's `unicode_words` does; `word_segments` keeps every piece, as its `split_word_bounds` does. ICU 78.3's word iterator cuts Chinese and Thai by its dictionaries ("漢字" one word, "ภาษาไทย" two, observed 2026-11-17); UAX #29's rules, these, give an ideograph and a Thai letter with its marks a piece each, since a Thai letter is Word_Break Other, and no dictionary of a language is carried

capability class/word-break  the class UAX #29 cuts words by
  heroes  unicode/segment.word_break_class
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    held to ICU 78.3's Word_Break on every scalar value by the generator and the sweep

